{"id":"mahabharata-12-278","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":278,"title":"अष्टसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 278 · Shukra, Kubera and the sage Jaigishavya","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks Bhishma to tell of Shukra, the son of Bhrigu, and Bhishma tells how Kubera's wealth was taken by Shiva's yogic power, how Shiva then became rich by austerity and wealth, and the tale of Devi's question to Shiva. He ends the account of the great-souled Bhargava.","kn":"ಭೃಗುವಿನ ಮಗ ಶುಕ್ರನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕುಬೇರನ ಸಂಪತ್ತನ್ನು ಶಿವ ಯೋಗಶಕ್ತಿಯಿಂದ ತೆಗೆದುಕೊಂಡದ್ದು, ಶಿವ ತಪಸ್ಸು-ಧನದಿಂದ ಶ್ರೀಮಂತನಾದುದು, ದೇವಿಯ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮಹಾತ್ಮ ಭಾರ್ಗವನ ಕಥೆ ಮುಗಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर भृगुपुत्र शुक्र के बारे में पूछते हैं, और भीष्म बताते हैं कि कुबेर का धन शिव ने योगशक्ति से ले लिया, शिव तप और धन से समृद्ध हुए और देवी ने उनसे प्रश्न किया। वे महात्मा भार्गव का वृत्तान्त समाप्त करते हैं।","te":"భృగుని కొడుకు శుక్రుని గురించి చెప్పమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; కుబేరుని సంపదను శివుడు యోగశక్తితో తీసుకున్న తీరు, శివుడు తపస్సు, ధనంతో సంపన్నుడైన తీరు, దేవి ప్రశ్నను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. మహాత్ముడైన భార్గవుని కథ ముగుస్తుంది.","ta":"பிருகுவின் மகன் சுக்ரனைப் பற்றிக் கூறுமாறு யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, குபேரனின் செல்வத்தைச் சிவன் யோக ஆற்றலால் எடுத்ததையும் சிவன் தவத்தாலும் செல்வத்தாலும் செழித்ததையும் தேவியின் கேள்வியையும் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். மகாத்மா பார்க்கவனின் கதையை முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ഭൃഗുവിന്റെ പുത്രനായ ശുക്രനെക്കുറിച്ച് പറയണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ഭീഷ്മരോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; കുബേരന്റെ ധനം ശിവന്റെ യോഗശക്തിയാൽ അപഹരിക്കപ്പെട്ടതും, പിന്നീട് തപസ്സിലൂടെയും സമ്പത്തിലൂടെയും ശിവൻ ധനികനായതും ഭീഷ്മർ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ദേവി ശിവനോട് ചോദിച്ച ചോദ്യത്തിന്റെ കഥയോടെ, മഹാത്മാവായ ഭാർഗവന്റെ വിവരണം അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.278; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तिष्ठते मे सदा तात कौतूहलमिदं हृदि ।\nतदहं श्रोतुमिच्छामि त्वत्तः कुरुपितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear grandfather of the Kurus, this curiosity always remains in my heart, and I wish to hear about it from you."}},{"n":2,"text":"कथं देवर्षिरुशना सदा काव्यो महामतिः ।\nअसुराणां प्रियकरः सुराणामप्रिये रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How is it that the divine sage Ushanas Kavya, of great intellect, always did what pleased the Asuras and delighted in what displeased the gods?"}},{"n":3,"text":"वर्धयामास तेजश्च किमर्थममितौजसाम् ।\nनित्यं वैरनिबद्धाश्च दानवाः सुरसत्तमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For what reason did he increase the power of those of boundless might, the Danavas, who were bound in constant enmity with the best of gods?"}},{"n":4,"text":"कथं चाप्युशना प्राप शुक्रत्वममरद्युतिः ।\nऋद्धिं च स कथं प्राप्तः सर्वमेतद्ब्रवीहि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how did Ushanas, radiant like the immortals, gain the name Shukra? And how did he gain his prosperity? Tell me all this."}},{"n":5,"text":"न याति च स तेजस्वी मध्येन नभसः कथम् ।\nएतदिच्छामि विज्ञातुं निखिलेन पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how is it that this brilliant one does not travel through the middle of the sky? Grandfather, I wish to know all this fully."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"शृणु राजन्नवहितः सर्वमेतद्यथातथम् ।\nयथामति यथा चैतच्छ्रुतपूर्वं मयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, listen attentively to all this as it truly happened, as I understand it and as I heard it before, sinless one."}},{"n":7,"text":"एष भार्गवदायादो मुनिः सत्यो दृढव्रतः ।\nअसुराणां प्रियकरो निमित्ते करुणात्मके ॥","meaning":{"en":"This sage, heir of Bhrigu, truthful and firm in his vows, does what pleases the Asuras when there is a compassionate cause."}},{"n":8,"text":"इन्द्रोऽथ धनदो राजा यक्षरक्षोधिपः स च ।\nप्रभविष्णुश्च कोशस्य जगतश्च तथा प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now there was a king, the giver of wealth, lord of Yakshas and Rakshasas, master of the treasury and ruler over the world too."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्यात्मानमथाविश्य योगसिद्धो महामुनिः ।\nरुद्ध्वा धनपतिं देवं योगेन हृतवान्वसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great sage, perfected in yoga, entered into his very self, held back the god, the lord of wealth, by yoga, and carried off his riches."}},{"n":10,"text":"हृते धने ततः शर्म न लेभे धनदस्तथा ।\nआपन्नमन्युः संविग्नः सोऽभ्यगात्सुरसत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When his wealth was taken, the giver of wealth found no peace; distressed and anguished, he went to the best of the gods."}},{"n":11,"text":"निवेदयामास तदा शिवायामिततेजसे ।\nदेवश्रेष्ठाय रुद्राय सौम्याय बहुरूपिणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he reported it to Shiva of boundless energy, Rudra, the best of the gods, gentle, of many forms."}},{"text":"कुबेर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kubera said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"योगात्मकेनोशनसा रुद्ध्वा मम हृतं वसु ।\nयोगेनात्मगतिं कृत्वा निःसृतश्च महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ushanas, whose very self is yoga, held me back and carried off my wealth. Having made himself one with me by yoga, that great ascetic has gone out."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा ततः क्रुद्धो महायोगी महेश्वरः ।\nसंरक्तनयनो राजञ्शूलमादाय तस्थिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, the great yogi Maheshvara grew angry. With reddened eyes, king, he took up his trident and stood ready."}},{"n":14,"text":"क्वास्वौ क्वासाविति प्राह गृहीत्वा परमायुधम् ।\nउशना दूरतस्तस्य बभौ ज्ञात्वा चिकीर्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seizing his supreme weapon he said, \"Where is he, where?\" But Ushanas, knowing his intention, shone from afar."}},{"n":15,"text":"स महायोगिनो बुद्ध्वा तं रोषं वै महात्मनः ।\nगतिमागमनं वेत्ति स्थानं वेत्ति ततः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the wrath of that great yogi, the lord Ushanas knew his movement, his approach and his place."}},{"n":16,"text":"संचिन्त्योग्रेण तपसा महात्मानं महेश्वरम् ।\nउशना योगसिद्धात्मा शूलाग्रे प्रत्यदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having meditated on the great Maheshvara with fierce austerity, Ushanas, whose self was perfected in yoga, appeared on the tip of the trident."}},{"n":17,"text":"विज्ञातरूपः स तदा तपःसिद्धेन धन्विना ।\nज्ञात्वा शूलं च देवेशः पाणिना समनामयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the lord of the gods, recognizing his form, the archer perfected in austerity, knew that it was the trident and bent it down with his hand."}},{"n":18,"text":"आनतेनाथ शूलेन पाणिनामिततेजसा ।\nपिनाकमिति चोवाच शूलमुग्रायुधः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the trident bent by his hand of boundless power, the fierce-weaponed lord called the trident \"Pinaka.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"पाणिमध्यगतं दृष्ट्वा भार्गवं तमुमापतिः ।\nआस्यं विवृत्य ककुदी पाणिं संप्राक्षिपच्छनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that son of Bhrigu in the middle of his palm, the husband of Uma, the humped bull-rider, opened his mouth and slowly threw his hand to it."}},{"n":20,"text":"स तु प्रविष्ट उशना कोष्ठं माहेश्वरं प्रभुः ।\nव्यचरच्चापि तत्रासौ महात्मा भृगुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Ushanas, the lord, entered Maheshvara's belly and the great son of Bhrigu wandered about in there."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"किमर्थं व्यचरद्राजन्नुशना तस्य धीमतः ।\nजठरे देवदेवस्य किं चाकार्षीन्महाद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why, king, did Ushanas wander in the belly of the wise god of gods, and what did that very radiant one do there?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"पुरा सोऽन्तर्जलगतः स्थाणुभूतो महाव्रतः ।\nवर्षाणामभवद्राजन्प्रयुतान्यर्बुदानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago the great-vowed god stayed under water, still as a post, for tens of millions and hundreds of millions of years."}},{"n":23,"text":"उदतिष्ठत्तपस्तप्त्वा दुश्चरं स महाह्रदात् ।\nततो देवातिदेवस्तं ब्रह्मा समुपसर्पत ॥","meaning":{"en":"After performing hard austerity he rose from the great lake; and then Brahma, god above gods, approached him."}},{"n":24,"text":"तपोवृद्धिमपृच्छच्च कुशलं चैनमव्ययम् ।\nतपः सुचीर्णमिति च प्रोवाच वृषभध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma asked about the growth of his austerity and his lasting well-being, and the bull-bannered god replied that the austerity had been well performed."}},{"n":25,"text":"तत्संयोगेन वृद्धिं चाप्यपश्यत्स तु शंकरः ।\nमहामतिरचिन्त्यात्मा सत्यधर्मरतः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shankara, of great mind and inconceivable nature, ever devoted to truth and dharma, also saw growth through that union."}},{"n":26,"text":"स तेनाढ्यो महायोगी तपसा च धनेन च ।\nव्यराजत महाराज त्रिषु लोकेषु वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rich in that austerity and that wealth, the great yogi, the mighty one, shone in the three worlds, great king."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततः पिनाकी योगात्मा ध्यानयोगं समाविशत् ।\nउशना तु समुद्विग्नो निलिल्ये जठरे ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Pinaka's bearer, yoga-souled, entered into meditation, and Ushanas, alarmed, hid himself in the belly."}},{"n":28,"text":"तुष्टाव च महायोगी देवं तत्रस्थ एव च ।\nनिःसारं काङ्क्षमाणस्तु तेजसा प्रत्यहन्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great yogi praised the god from where he was, and wanting a way out, was struck back by the god's radiance."}},{"n":29,"text":"उशना तु तदोवाच जठरस्थो महामुनिः ।\nप्रसादं मे कुरुष्वेति पुनः पुनररिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great sage Ushanas, in the belly, said again and again, \"Be gracious to me,\" subduer of foes."}},{"n":30,"text":"तमुवाच महादेवो गच्छ शिश्नेन मोक्षणम् ।\nइति स्रोतांसि सर्वाणि रुद्ध्वा त्रिदशपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahadeva told him, \"Go out by the organ of generation,\" having blocked all the other channels, the bull among the gods."}},{"n":31,"text":"अपश्यमानः स द्वारं सर्वतःपिहितो मुनिः ।\nपर्यक्रामद्दह्यमान इतश्चेतश्च तेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not seeing a door, the sage, shut in on every side, circled about, burning here and there with that radiance."}},{"n":32,"text":"स विनिष्क्रम्य शिश्नेन शुक्रत्वमभिपेदिवान् ।\nकार्येण तेन नभसो नागच्छत च मध्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He came out by the organ of generation and gained the name Shukra; for that reason he does not go through the middle of the sky."}},{"n":33,"text":"निष्क्रान्तमथ तं दृष्ट्वा ज्वलन्तमिव तेजसा ।\nभवो रोषसमाविष्टः शूलोद्यतकरः स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him come out, blazing as it were with energy, Bhava, filled with rage, stood with raised trident in hand."}},{"n":34,"text":"न्यवारयत तं देवी क्रुद्धं पशुपतिं पतिम् ।\nपुत्रत्वमगमद्देव्या वारिते शंकरे च सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The goddess restrained her angry husband, Pashupati; and once Shankara was restrained by the goddess, Ushanas became her son."}},{"text":"देव्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"The goddess said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"हिंसनीयस्त्वया नैष मम पुत्रत्वमागतः ।\nन हि देवोदरात्कश्चिन्निःसृतो नाशमर्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"You must not harm him, for he has become my son; no one who has come out of the god's belly deserves to be destroyed."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः प्रीतोऽभवद्देव्याः प्रहसंश्चेदमब्रवीत् ।\nगच्छत्वेष यथाकाममिति राजन्पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the god was pleased with the goddess and, laughing, said again and again, king, \"Let him go as he wishes.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः प्रणम्य वरदं देवं देवीमुमां तथा ।\nउशना प्राप तद्धीमान्गतिमिष्टां महामुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, bowing to the boon-giving god and to the goddess Uma, the wise great sage Ushanas reached the goal he desired."}},{"n":38,"text":"एतत्ते कथितं तात भार्गवस्य महात्मनः ।\nचरितं भरतश्रेष्ठ यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear one, I have told you the story of the great son of Bhrigu, best of the Bharatas, which you asked me about."}}]}]}